<ansi fg="black-bold">.:</ansi> <ansi fg="magenta">Help for </ansi><ansi fg="command">wizard-routes</ansi>

A wizard promotes at level 10 to one of four advanced classes, and at level 30
to the elite class that continues its route (<ansi fg="command">help promotion</ansi>).

<ansi fg="yellow-bold">Theurgist</ansi> (good, alignment +30)  protective arcane support
  10 Arcane Ward      one ally's next blow is absorbed, up to one average hit
                      (chant 1, cost 10, one ward per ally)
  15 Steady chant     blows break its chant 25% less often
  20 Double ward      a ward absorbs two blows
  25 Deep reserves    +10% maximum mana
  Elite: Archon (<ansi fg="command">help archon</ansi>)

<ansi fg="yellow-bold">Arcanist</ansi> (neutral)  reliable damage and mana-efficient casting
  10 Arcane focus     spells deal 10% more damage
  15 Efficient casting spells cost 10% less mana
  20 Sharper focus    spells deal 15% more damage
  25 Steady chant     blows break its chant 25% less often
  Elite: Archmage (<ansi fg="command">help archmage</ansi>)

<ansi fg="yellow-bold">Sorcerer</ansi> (neutral)  costly magical burst: one heavy Arcane Lance at a time
  10 Arcane Lance     a heavy bolt at one foe, about twice a Magic Missile
                      (chant 2 rounds, cost 15)
  15 Gathered power   the Lance deals 25% more damage
  20 Steady chant     blows break its chant 25% less often
  25 Cheaper lance    the Lance costs 12
  Elite: High Sorcerer (<ansi fg="command">help high-sorcerer</ansi>)

<ansi fg="yellow-bold">Warlock</ansi> (evil, alignment -30)  life-draining magic
  10 Life Drain       damages one foe for a Magic Missile's worth and heals the
                      most hurt ally for the damage dealt (chant 1, cost 10)
  15 Cheaper drain    Life Drain costs 8
  20 Twin drain       Life Drain also strikes a second foe and heals a second
                      ally, at 60%
  25 Dark focus       spells deal 10% more damage
  Elite: Necromancer (<ansi fg="command">help necromancer</ansi>)

A wizard's role is caster (<ansi fg="command">help strategy</ansi>): it casts on its own, a Theurgist
wards the company first, and a Sorcerer looses its Lance first for as long as
its mana lasts, then falls back to Magic Missile.

See also: <ansi fg="command">help classes</ansi>, <ansi fg="command">help elite</ansi>, <ansi fg="command">help talents</ansi>, <ansi fg="command">help strategy</ansi>.
